  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nNow Tropical Depression Edouard will stay well northeast through \nWednesday night as it weakens into northeast Texas. South Texas \nsurface moisture will increase along the Coastal Bend today along \nwith sunshine, but subsidence will negate mentionable rain chances. \nHowever, a Heat Advisory has been issued for inland Kleberg, Nueces, \nand San Patricio Counties where heat indices of 110 or more for at \nleast 2 hours is expected this afternoon. This area is highlighted \nin the 40-50% HREF probabilities for apparent temperatures at least \n110 degrees. Each afternoon, heat will remain our primary concern, \nwith WBGT UIL risks moderate to high areawide. \n\nModels are in good agreement of the ridge over SE CONUS shoving the \nremnants of Edouard southwestward over South Texas Thursday into \nFriday, lingering through Labor Day Weekend. The additional lift \nsupport from the remnants along with climbing PWAT values nearing \n2.0\" and the seabreeze, will allow for a low to medium (20-40%) \nchance of showers and thunderstorms. Greatest chances and confidence \nresides over the Victoria Crossroads where PVA is maximized and \nmoisture is expected to be greatest.\n\nOutside of the heat and low rain chances, elevated fire weather \nconditions are a concern this afternoon and evening over the Brush \nCountry. Additional information is below in the fire weather \ndiscussion.",
